  "caps": [
    "To an AI, every word is a point in space.",
    "A sentence is a path. The next word: a calculation, then a roll of the dice.",
    "I wanted to understand AI. I found math.",
    "So I looked up.",
    "And everywhere I looked, calculations.",
    "The sea: simple waves adding up.",
    "A flower: each seed at 137.5° from the last.",
    "It never learned math. It's the solution that survived.",
    "Closer.",
    "In every seed, a code. Four letters, read three at a time.",
    "And deep down, nature rolls the dice.",
    "The world can be calculated. It can't be predicted.",
    "Spirals, from the flower to the galaxy.",
    "What if the universe were just one big algorithm?",
    "And me? Signals between 86 billion neurons.",
    "A neuron adds up the signals it receives, each with its own weight. An artificial neuron does the same math.",
    "And my brain spends its time predicting what comes next. Like an LLM.",
    "Am I an AI?",
    "Not an LLM. A body that learned to speak last.",
    "A body that keeps itself going, and feels.",
    "What if we retraced it all, in one go?",
    "The complexity of life, fast-forwarded.",
    "And it all comes down to this: an atom.",
    "Electricity, flowing.",
    "In a neuron.",
    "In an AI's parameters.",
    "If everything is calculation, why does it feel like something to be me?"
  ],
